schema: test/v2
level: working-unit
epic: E-REDESIGN
wu: E-REDESIGN.W4
tests:
  unit:
    count: 26
    covers: |
      ui/src/FlowList.test.tsx — 15 tests, a NEW FILE: this screen was the only one in ui/src/ with no adjacent test, which the epic plan names as a row to close. Each asserts what the design DECLARES. Cells: the verb carries its tone class, the time is an absolute HH:MM:SS clock, the status pill's accessible name carries its reason phrase ("200 OK"), and a pending flow's DurationText renders the invisible fixed-width placeholder rather than collapsing the column. Absences: the two causes are checked AGAINST EACH OTHER — each test asserts the other sentence is absent, because one message serving both is the defect Tune T3 removed. Keyboard: one tab stop with aria-activedescendant; arrows move by one; NEITHER WRAPS (both ends); either arrow into an unselected list lands on the first row (the design's stated Select convention, both directions); Enter and Space each open; the pointer path still works. Truncation: host and path carry truncate AND the row carries the full path as its title — both halves, so a later "fix" that drops the title fails. Windowing: a 200-row list is driven past the rendered window and the virtualizer is asserted to be ASKED to follow at every step (see the note for what jsdom cannot prove).
      ui/src/useFlows.test.ts — 2 new tests for the host accumulation the filter dropdown reads. A host STAYS ON OFFER after the filter narrows the list away from it (the whole reason the options are accumulated rather than derived from `flows`, which is server-filtered), and a URI with no parseable host contributes no option. Added after a review pointed out the behaviour was only covered through the full App tree.
      ui/src/flow.test.ts — updated to FlowRow's reduced shape: toRow returns exactly {host, path}, asserted by key set, because the four other values must reach their components raw.
      ui/src/App.test.tsx — 6 new. The count renders through TonedText at muted (Tune T2). The method dropdown offers the verbs and NOT a partial verb, which is the exactness the design flagged. Host options include a host absent from the currently filtered list. The status control is still an INPUT — the deferral asserted, so a later half-conversion is visible. Plus the two integration rows below.
  integration:
    count: 4
    covers: "ui/src/App.test.tsx — the bounded contract is the screen against a live API, over a fake TrawlerApi whose listFlows now mirrors FlowFilter::matches closely enough for these fixtures (host and q as substrings; the comment states where it diverges rather than overclaiming). Four paths cross the App/FlowList seam: a proven launch with no traffic renders the nothing-captured absence and NOT the filter one; choosing a host from the dropdown narrows to it and 'any host' restores the list, with SSE appending afterwards; a free-text query matching nothing renders the filter absence and NOT the launch one; and the keyboard alone (ArrowDown x2, Enter) opens the second row's detail, asserted by getFlow being called with f2 — the seam matters because FlowList owns the keys while App owns the selection and the fetch."
  e2e:
    count: 19
    covers: "cargo xtask ui e2e — 19/19 specs, 2 files. NOT waived: this WU changes rendered screens. A NEW UC-4 block (9 specs) implements the epic e2e plan's UC-4 row against the real WebKit window: a proxied request lands carrying an absolute time, a toned verb and a duration; the status pill carries its reason phrase; the method dropdown offers the verbs and not a partial verb; a filter narrows the list; an unmatched filter shows the filter absence and NOT the launch one; clearing restores the rows; the host dropdown offers the host capture actually saw (matched by prefix, since the harness origin is localhost on an ephemeral port) and choosing it narrows; the header's three controls are MEASURED as sharing one top edge, so the row does not wrap and Select's 132px floor survives the caller's width; and the keyboard alone selects a row and opens its detail, focused via browser.execute rather than a click so the assertion is about the keys. onboarding.spec.ts's filter spec moved to the free-text key, since an unmatchable host is no longer expressible in a dropdown of hosts that were actually seen. UC-5's 6 specs stay green unchanged, which is why they could not be this WU's proof: they assert on data-testids this WU deliberately preserved."
verified:
  - "cd ui && pnpm test — 551 passed, 43 files, 0 failed (527 before this WU)."
  - "cargo xtask ui e2e — 19/19 across 2 spec files, against the real Tauri/WebKit window and an ephemeral core."
  - "cd ui && pnpm exec eslint src — silent. The closed-vocabulary lint (DEC-17) is what proves text-center and flex-wrap are declared members rather than classes resolving to nothing."
  - "npx tsc -b — clean over FlowRow's reduced shape, the filtered prop and the new hosts/HTTP_METHODS exports."
  - "cargo test && cargo xtask gate0 — green. No Rust changed; re-walked because the gate does."
  - "node scripts/design-registry.mjs — 27 entries after the two TSDoc edits; the oracle throws on a block missing a tag, so a malformed contract cannot pass silently."
  - "cargo xtask design-scope epic/redesign HEAD — five rendered files: three cited to W3's design, two (MethodLabel, Select) declared undesigned as TSDoc-only edits with their reasons."
  - "cargo xtask verify-doc on both docs/work/2026-09-05-redesign-w4-plan.html and -w4-result.html — green."
note: "THE E2E ASSERTIONS ARE THE ONES THAT MATTER, because each FAILS AGAINST THE PRE-WU BUILD: the reason phrase in the pill's accessible name, the filter absence's own sentence, the dropdowns, and a keyboard path that did not exist at all (the row was a div with an onClick carrying aria-selected on nothing). A UC-4 block written against the testids this screen already had would have passed green while proving nothing — the trap the epic plan names when it says the preserved testids cannot be the epic's proof. WHAT THE UNIT LAYER CANNOT PROVE, stated rather than implied: jsdom implements no scrollTo, and the virtualizer's scroll-into-view IS a scrollElement.scrollTo call, so under jsdom the window provably cannot follow. The 200-row test asserts the virtualizer is ASKED at every step including past the window's edge, and its comment says so; the browser honouring it is the e2e's assertion. THAT GAP WAS A REVIEW FINDING: every keyboard test originally used a 3-row fixture fitting the mocked 600px viewport whole, so the virtualizer never windowed and the mechanism — which exists precisely so the keyboard path is not nominal — could have been deleted with the suite green. TWO OTHER FIRST-ROUND FINDINGS were real and fixed: the empty state hardcoded 127.0.0.1:7420 where api.ts's own comment forbids it (DEC-12), so under VITE_TRAWLER_PROXY the list and onboarding would have disagreed — the test now asserts against defaultProxyAddr() so it cannot re-freeze; and the design's wire-markup line asks for data-wire on all six payload cells plus the region and header chrome, of which only two cells had it. A SECOND REVIEW RAN over the filter change (two finders, three findings, all fixed): the nine-verb set was a third copy, now exported from MethodLabel which owns verb semantics; Select's @avoid gained the any-option clause so the next clearable filter finds the pattern in the contract rather than copying it out of App.tsx; and the mock's comment claimed to mirror FlowFilter::matches when the server matches host against the parsed authority and the mock substring-matches the whole URI — the fixtures make them agree, which is what it now says. Both reviewers cleared the substance: the accumulation's early return, the NUL-prefixed ANY sentinel, empty-string handling end to end, and Select's contract under the any-option pattern. THE TRUNCATION IS DELIBERATE AND TESTED AS SUCH: host and path truncate because a virtualized fixed-height row cannot wrap, which W3 recorded as a narrow violation paid for by the row's title and the detail pane, escalated to W11 because the rulebook has no clause for it. The rulebook is unmoved (aeff5b0), so that verdict is unchanged."
